.TH GETATTR 5
.SH NAME
getattr, setattr \- inquire or change file attributes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B size[4] Tgetattr tag[2] fid[4] request_mask[8]
.B size[4] Rgetattr tag[2] valid[8] qid[13] mode[4] uid[4] gid[4]
.B nlink[8] rdev[8] size[8] blksize[8] blocks[8]
.B atime_sec[8] atime_nsec[8] mtime_sec[8] mtime_nsec[8]
.B ctime_sec[8] ctime_nsec[8] btime_sec[8] btime_nsec[8]
.B gen[8] data_version[8]
.fi
.PP
.nf
.B size[4] Tsetattr tag[2] fid[4] valid[4] mode[4] uid[4] gid[4] size[8]
.B atime_sec[8] atime_nsec[8] mtime_sec[8] mtime_nsec[8]
.B size[4] Rsetattr tag[2]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tgetattr
asks for the fields named in
.IR request_mask ,
a bit for each field.
.B GETATTR_BASIC,
0x7ff, is what every Vectra server answers, and is the mask
.IR stat (2)
sends.
The reply's
.I valid
says which fields the server actually filled in,
and it may be fewer than were asked for:
a caller that reads a field without checking
.I valid
is reading whatever the server happened to leave there.
.PP
The fields, once
.I valid
says they are there:
.TP
.I qid
the server's identity for the file
.TP
.I mode
Linux's file-type and permission bits
.TP
.I uid
the owner, as a number
.TP
.I gid
the group, as a number
.TP
.I nlink
the number of names the file has
.TP
.I size
length in bytes
.TP
.I blksize
the block size a caller should read or write in
.TP
.I blocks
the file's length in those blocks
.TP
.I atime, mtime, ctime, btime
access, modification, status-change and creation times,
each a pair of seconds and nanoseconds since the epoch
.TP
.I gen
a generation number
.TP
.I data_version
a version counter, for a caller that wants to notice a file changed
underneath it
.PD
.PP
.B Tsetattr
changes the fields named in
.IR valid ,
a different, narrower set of bits than
.BR Tgetattr 's
.IR request_mask .
Vectra's servers implement two of them:
.B SETATTR_MODE
(0x1) for
.I mode
and
.B SETATTR_SIZE
(0x8) for
.I size,
which truncates or extends the file.
A bit for a field a server does not implement is refused rather than
silently ignored.
.PP
A server over a fixed, read-only tree refuses
.B Tsetattr
outright, with
.BR EROFS .
.SH SOURCE
.B sys/vectra9/proto.odin
.br
.B kernel/vfs/chan.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR intro (5),
.IR open (5),
.IR read (5),
.IR vectra9 (2)
